{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790964408,"nonce":"lKIgbbJwwYNjUiFhjjMX5mzy+Jk=","message":"Landed as `git work quickstart`, markdown on stdout, no argument and no flag.\n\nTwo halves in one call, so that reading it once is enough to write a document\n`issue new` accepts:\n\n- The static guide, `host/quickstart.md`, embedded with `//go:embed`: what\n  git-work is, how it is stored (an entity per issue, a DAG of operations\n  under its own ref, a CRDT merged by fetch and push; ids, prefixes, aliases;\n  the four namespaces; the authoring files are not the truth, the refs are),\n  the command model (plumbing, JSON in and out, new/get/set/add/remove,\n  comment, log, archive, rm, `--dry-run`, the schema check that reports every\n  problem at once, the jq listing), where everything it leaves out is (schema,\n  `--help`, flows, views need a TTY, the Starlark mirror, sync, `user me`),\n  what each field kind accepts, and five worked examples.\n- The live half, assembled by `host.Quickstart`: one section per type in the\n  store, each field as `key (kind[: values | -\u003e target types; read back as\n  inverse])`, the three built-ins named once in the guide rather than on\n  every type. An empty store says so and names `schema init`.\n\n`work.quickstart()` returns the same string, a verb on the `work` module\nitself, the way a root command is a verb on the binary.\n\nThe markdown lives in `host/`, not `commands/`, because `host` is what\nassembles the two halves and `commands` imports `host`, never the reverse.\n\nTests: `commands/quickstart_test.go` covers the empty-store sentence and the\nlive types of an imported schema, and walks the cobra tree for every command\nthe output spells out, so one renamed or dropped fails the build rather than\nsending an agent after a verb that is gone (it reads code spans and code-block\nlines only -- prose words are shaped exactly like command names).\n`flow/run` pins `work.quickstart()` against `host.Quickstart`.","files":null}]}